<title>Camset Editor: third-party licences</title>
<!-- Written by cargo about from editor/about.hbs and editor/about.toml; do not edit. -->
<style>
  :root { --bg: #fff; --fg: #1d1d1f; --muted: #6e6e73; --box: #f5f5f7; --line: #d2d2d7; --link: #0066cc; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root { --bg: #1c1c1e; --fg: #f5f5f7; --muted: #a1a1a6; --box: #2c2c2e; --line: #3a3a3c; --link: #4da3ff; }
  }
  body { background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); font: 15px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; margin: 0; padding: 0 16px; }
  main { max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 0 48px; }
  a { color: var(--link); }
  p, .count { color: var(--muted); }
  section { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); margin-top: 28px; }
  ul.crates { columns: 3 14em; padding-left: 1.2em; }
  pre { background: var(--box); padding: 12px; overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre-wrap; font-size: 13px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<h1>Third-party licences</h1>
<p>Camset Editor is built from the Rust crates below. Each licence's text follows, with the crates it covers.
The fonts that egui builds in (crate epaint_default_fonts) are listed under their own licences: Ubuntu Light and
Noto Emoji under the crate's, and Hack and the emoji icon font, whose notices the crate carries beside the fonts,
at the end.</p>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}
  <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> <span class="count">({{count}})</span></li>
{{/each}}
  <li><a href="#font-hack">Hack font: MIT License and Bitstream Vera License</a></li>
  <li><a href="#font-emoji-icon">Emoji icon font: MIT License</a></li>
</ul>
{{!-- the editor's own crate (camset-editor, MIT, the repository's LICENSE) is left out: the page is for the others --}}
{{#each licenses}}
<section>
  <h2 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h2>
  <ul class="crates">
  {{#each used_by}}{{#unless (eq crate.name "camset-editor")}}
    <li><a href="https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a></li>
  {{/unless}}{{/each}}
  </ul>
  <pre>{{text}}</pre>
</section>
{{/each}}
{{!-- The fonts epaint_default_fonts builds in whose licences its Cargo.toml does not declare, so cargo about does not
list them: the notices the crate carries (fonts/Hack-Regular.txt, fonts/emoji-icon-font-mit-license.txt), as written. --}}
